==Enemy==
Bun Bun Symbiote is very similar to the original [[Teacher Bun Bun]], but has higher health and attack power, lower speed and only five knockbacks. While he still only has 200 range, Bun Bun Symbiote also gains a 5% chance to generate a Level 1 [[Wave Attack]] that extends his reach to 467.5, which can demolish groups of short- to mid-ranged units when it occurs and allow him to suddenly advance.

==Strategy==
As with [[J.K. Bun Bun]] and [[Bun Bun Black]], you should exploit his dual-trait weakness, using whatever [[:Category:Anti-Floating Cats|anti-Floating]] and [[:Category:Anti-Alien Cats|anti-Alien]] crowd-control units you can (such as [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Castaway Cat]], [[Shaman Cat (Rare Cat)|Necromancer Cat]], [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cat]], and [[Psychocat (Rare Cat)|Neo Psychocat]]) to delay or paralyze him, ensuring he doesn't fire off waves when he hits your meatshields, and use specialist attackers to quickly remove him before he becomes a threat. His low Wave chance and level mean that [[:Category:Cats with Wave Immunity|Wave-immune]]/[[:Category:Wave Shield Cats|Wave Shield]] units are generally not worth bringing solely for the purpose of fighting him, but specialists like [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Butterfly Cat]] and [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] can still capitalize on such abilities with either speed or utility.

